# Project: Go Root CA API Server (step-ca SDK based)

## Core Directives
- **Language:** All code, variables, strictly technical documentation, and code comments MUST be written in English.
- **Completeness:** ALWAYS implement all functions and modules completely. NEVER use placeholders, `// TODO`, or mock implementations. Do not leave any code for the user to write.
- **Tech Stack:** Use Go 1.22+. Use the standard library `net/http` for routing (utilizing the new Go 1.22 multiplexer features). Avoid unnecessary third-party web frameworks to keep the binary lean and secure.
- **PKI Engine:** Use `github.com/smallstep/certificates` and `github.com/smallstep/cli` Go SDKs for the underlying CA mechanics.
- **Tone & Style:** Professional, highly technical, concise, and forward-thinking.

## Architecture Guidelines
- Follow Domain-Driven Design (DDD) principles: separate Handlers (API), Services (Business Logic), and Repositories (Data/CA Engine).
- Standardize all API JSON responses. Include an `error` field (null if successful) and a `data` field.
- Ensure robust, contextual error handling. Log internally, but return sanitized error messages via the API.

## Future-Proofing
- The API will eventually serve a WebUI. Keep endpoints RESTful and stateless.
- Any future frontend code or HTML/CSS templates MUST default to a dark mode, flat, modern UI aesthetic.